A||||43||DaRkLoRD||incorrect Fiero badging... rice??||||5||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||01-10-2001||03:58 AM||||I've seen a few Fieros that have been modified in ways that might seem "ricey". I saw a coupe, 4cyl exhaust tips and rear fascia, but it had a GT badge stuck on it... couldn't determine the front fascia, as the car had a bra on. It was missing the aux gauge cluster as well.<BR>There are a few other examples I've seen in the last couple of years, ranging from fake Indys, to fake Formulas..<P>I'm just curious as to how people regard this, compared to when "ricers" swap body panels on their cars from a better model of that car, or put a VTEC sticker on a car without a VTEC. To me, a GT badge on a 4cyl Fiero is the same thing...<P>Assuming I had an 84-85 Duke that I wanted to improve the looks of, the furthest I would go, is putting some aero ground effects/fascias/trim and wing on it, as well as some new wheels. I wouldn't change the sail panels though, and I'd get rid of the "Fiero 2M4" on the back of the decklid completely simply because I don't really like the way it looks.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry for the long post, I'm just wondering what other people think about this stuff..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shunyata||01-10-2001||04:51 AM||||imho...<BR>i see your point, and agree with the rice bit... but, they must like it or think it's 'cool' or they wouldnt have done it, and since its their car, and they're the ones who have to drive it/have it parked in their driveway, what they think about it is all that really matters.<P>------------------<BR>-Shun<BR>86.5 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||01-10-2001||05:00 AM||||I wouldn't call it ricing since the four cylinder has been in the GT/SE style (not counting the Indy style body) WITH the V6 exhaust (twin double exhaust) from the factory. Some 85 coupe bodies came with V6 (SE) and had the 2M6 on the trunklid.<BR>Fake Formulas? 87/88 coupes were 4 cylinders with the Formula body (or vice versa). Fieros with different body styles couldn't possibly be called rice since they can't change body styles to the extent that we can. <P>As far as the GT badge...perhaps the badge came on the replacement bumper from damage...or maybe you really should check under the trunk lid...With all the things we owners are doing to these Fieros, you might be looking at someone's project!<P>As for me, I've always liked the Formula styling from the first coupe I had. When it was destroyed the 85 GT I got was banged up so while I was replacing damaged body panels I changed the front and back to Formula. Haven't had time to change the rest of the GT cladding to Formula but it doesn't look bad in black. There now you aren't the one with the longest winded post!||||reg||6
Z||000003||BN Boomer||01-10-2001||06:06 AM||||My GT doesn't have, and to the best of my knowledge never did have, the aux gauge cluster. Does that make it ricey?||||reg||1
Z||000004||count_iblis||01-10-2001||08:05 AM||||Rice all the way. I hate that word.  It is so racist.  Only put stickers or badges on your car of what it really is.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||01-10-2001||09:41 AM||||i once saw a car that had the following:<BR>85 GT quarter windows<BR>SE trunk/markings on rear trunk<BR>Indy Paint<BR>Aero front bumper<BR>SE rims<BR>tan interior<BR>new v6<P>i forget the mileage, but they were asking $2300 for the car, and you couldn't even tell what it really was... other than it was a 84 or '85 (no 3rd brake lite)!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000006||firstfiero||01-10-2001||10:33 AM||||    Befor I had a fiero I was and still am a bmw enthusiast. Bmws special vehicles are called M class. If you went to a show they had what they called the M police because of this same thing. Guys dressing up their cars and putting the right kind of engine in it and then badging it as an m class. The M police would come around and check your vin numbers and if they found out you had a fake m class they would throw you out of the show. the problem this brings comes in dishonesty of these owners when selling their car...pretending like they have an m class and then selling it as such. That's where I have a problem. I was thinking about putting gt symbols on my se...but changed my mind because in my mind oppionion it's ricer....but that's just me. Do what you like.86se||||reg||1
Z||000007||jerpro||01-10-2001||11:01 AM||||If you make a car look like what it's not by simply adding stickers It is ricey, period.<BR>Isn't that probably the main reason we laugh at ricers?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||TheFiero64||01-10-2001||11:11 AM||||I wonder if it would be incorrect to add a formula sticker to my 88. It has a v6, the 120 speedo, center gauges, 15 inch wheels, & the wing.<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||jerpro||01-10-2001||11:40 AM||||If it's not a formula, don't put it.||||reg||1
Z||000010||GeeDee86GT||01-10-2001||11:56 AM||||Geez. It the 'standards police' thing.  Once you add/remove anything your car is no longer 'stock'. Bad thing? Nah. Dress it up how YOU like it. Of course, not everyone will like or accept it. It's only wrong if you alter your car to look like another model in order to fool a buyer into paying for a more 'expensive' car. Fraud? I think so!  Have fun with your ride. I will!<BR>Gary||||reg||8
Z||000011||TheFiero64||01-10-2001||12:04 PM||||I wouldn't add the sticker anyway. I was just wondering what the group thought.||||reg||1
Z||000012||fiero56||01-10-2001||12:12 PM||||One of my original intentions was that when I repainted my '86SE(hasn't been painted yet) was to mock it up similar to an Indy. I have decided, and I want to know what others think here, is what if I painted the car black with silver ground effects(non-Indy color), left the sliver 14" tech wheels on, and slapped white Indy door decals on? It would never be confused with a real Indy by Fiero enthusiasts, since the colors are wrong, as well as the engine, raly guages, wheels, etc. I would leave the interior stock '86. I think it would be kinda' neat, I have this thing for black cars, would be "the Indy I can never find cheap", etc.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||rogergarrison||01-10-2001||12:19 PM||||my 86 SE has a ferrari body, interior. so should I leave off all the Ferrari badging???? nope. its got it all including a Ferrari VIN plate, the real ones still there too. If I ever sold it, id think the buyer would be able to see its a replica, wouldnt try to sell it as a 'Ferrari'<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Tigger||01-10-2001||12:35 PM||||Pretty sure the only "GT" badge on mine is on the horn button of my Grant GT steering wheel.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  However, I've got indy badges on the lower part of the fenders.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>This question also arises when people put "SS" badges on chevy muscle cars that were originally camaros, malibus, etc.  It opens a can of worms everytime.<P>It's pretty much up the owner and what they want to do.<P>Fiero56, Sounds like a neat idea, but can you have the indy door decal made in silver to kinda go with the wheels and lower trim?<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue3.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||01-10-2001||03:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BN Boomer:<BR><B>My GT doesn't have, and to the best of my knowledge never did have, the aux gauge cluster. Does that make it ricey?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No, of course not.. I'm just saying this was a non-GT, with a GT badge.. it still had the coupe rear fascia and decklid.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||DaRkLoRD||01-10-2001||03:42 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TheFiero64:<BR><B>I wonder if it would be incorrect to add a formula sticker to my 88. It has a v6, the 120 speedo, center gauges, 15 inch wheels, & the wing.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Depending on the suspension, it'd basically a Formula.. but technically it's not. Though with all of those mods, it'd be a lot less of a big deal to put a formula sticker on than if you still had a stock 88 coupe.<P>To everyone: I wasn't intending any flames towards anyone or their cars, I just want to see what your opinions are on this topic..<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000017||ChadMan||01-10-2001||03:53 PM||||I don't know why, but I think it's kind of dishonest to rebadge a Coupe as a Formula, even with the engine upgrade and other mods (just as I think it's dishonest to rebadge a '67 Tempest as a GTO, or a '65 Mustang 2+2 as a GT350).<P>If you've done enough mods that you feel your car warrants a new model designation, why not borrow one from newer Pontiacs?  A Fiero GT with a turbo might be a Fiero GTP.  A Fiero SE with a 3.8 might be an SSE.  This is creative, attracts attention at shows, and is not dishonest in any way.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Songman||01-10-2001||04:08 PM||||Personally, I build my cars for me. People may not like what I do but they are my cars and I am the one that has to drive them.<P>People thought I was crazy for taking the stock engine out of my 70k mile Monte Carlo SS Aerocoupe and replacing it with a brand new 454 crate motor. Did it hurt the value? Who cares? It's my car and built for me.<P>Most people on the board have seen me acting so happy about getting the Indy from Doug. Since that time I have decided not to sell my white 88 coupe but to turn it into an Indy clone. A car with 88 suspension, bigger motor, but with an Indy paint job and lettering. Am I trying to pretend it's an Indy? No. But I can do things to it that I would not do to the Indy, like change the motor and other mods. Anyone that knows will be able to tell it is not an Indy by looking at many aspects of the car, for instance, the engine cover will have a hump in it...<P>I recently sold a Pontiac Historical documented 1969 Ram Air IV GTO Judge. One of only 237 made with a 4-speed. Every time I have ever been to a show or a cruise or anything I see fake Judges. Very easy to spot, especially if someone has done it to a LeMans. Just look for the 237 instead of the 242 in the VIN. But the point is, it didn't bother me. It didn't make my car worth any less. Cars are supposed to be fun. Do whatever you want to with them. If you want to 'rice' it up, go for it.<P>And I would bet that in a couple of years when I have my Indy and my Indy clone sitting side by side, a lot of people will like the clone better because it will have more cool things than the real one. Some purists may get upset but I think they should just lighten up... they are toys. Have fun!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||Will||01-10-2001||04:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jerpro:<BR><B>If it's not a formula, don't put it.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>    Befor I had a fiero I was and still am a bmw enthusiast. Bmws special vehicles are called M class. If you went to a show they had what they called the M police because of this same thing. Guys dressing up their cars and putting the right kind of engine in it and then badging it as an m class. The M police would come around and check your vin numbers and if they found out you had a fake m class they would throw you out of the show. the problem this brings comes in dishonesty of these owners when selling their car...pretending like they have an m class and then selling it as such. That's where I have a problem. I was thinking about putting gt symbols on my se...but changed my mind because in my mind oppionion it's ricer....but that's just me. Do what you like.86se</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I don't like putting up level badges on a car that is not up level. However, in a car that has the performance upgrades (e.g. '88 coupe with swaybar, V6, fascia, etc.), call it a Formula; so what if the VIN says it's a coupe.<P>BMW has a reputation for running something of a Gestapo around its cars. If a guy wants to take his 315, put a Motorsport spec engine, suspension, body panels, and wheels (and whatever else goes with and M3) on it, what real difference is there between that car and an M3? Only the VIN, provided he has put all the stuff on it.<BR>If I were in the market for an M3 I wouldn't care if it were an original or not, as long as it had the performance.<P>However, putting an M3 badge, body panels and wheels on a tired and otherwise stock 315 REALLY IS Rice.<P>Personally, I'd rather buy a 330xi, buy a supercharger kit and suspension mods and STILL have more money in my pocket than if I had bought an M3, AND have better performance to boot.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Philphine||01-10-2001||04:57 PM||||don't know. dont care. what about those emblems haze was talking about from the firebirds? i'm meaning to stop by a dealer and get one if they have them. it will become the badge on my '87. or the ram air emblems orief has on his indy scoop? it's called personalization. the whole fake indy or formula thing might be a different story, maybe, depending on motives, but i'm not judging what anyone dose to their car. ||||reg||1
Z||000021||FieroLisa||01-10-2001||05:33 PM||||Hey, a person can do whatever they want to their car- long as they don't care if other people talk about them. If a person has a coupe with whatever body changes and a GT badge, how do you know they didn't throw a 2.8 in there anyway? <BR>I don't think its right or wrong to do anything to a car. It's a persons choice to do it and it's our choice to have an opinion on it, whether we express it or not.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR>*As Always, Updated Website*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000022||jerpro||01-10-2001||05:34 PM||||The base idea of making a car look what it's not, makes it ricey.<BR>If all you are doing is personalizing the car I have nothing against that.<BR>About the white fiero. It is a cool project, But I would of grabbed an indy and restored it instead.<BR>Basically the fake indy is a great car BUT I am against it. (this is opinion, no flame war intended)<BR>You have a 88 coupe and make mods to it, GREAT! But don't lable it a formula because it is NOT a formula.<BR>I have also read that "well, other fiero owners know it's not a formula" But the truth is that there are a lot of people that don't understand fieros and will take it as a real fiero formula. Basically this is lying. <BR>Even if you don't sell it.<BR>Sorry I am how I am, but I don't want fieros to get labled ricey. I had the option of buying a civic or a fiero and I went for the fiero simply because It does not have the reputation of being a ricey car.<BR>Next thing you know people will go up to your real formula and actually Question you if it is a real formula, because they will know that there are fiero owners out there that do change their cars to look like something they are not.<BR>again, no flame war intended.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.||||reg||1
Z||000023||88formula||01-10-2001||05:44 PM|||| I ate rice last night and it was good! ||||reg||1
Z||000024||TheFiero64||01-10-2001||06:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B> I ate rice last night and it was good! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Was it white,Fried,or another type?<P><P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||12
Z||000025||Cheever2||01-10-2001||07:23 PM||||My problem with ricers is the extra effort made to intentionally deceive.  It's not illegal, no, but some of us desire to say we don't like it as a trend.  <P>Is it ricey to make a kit-car?  No.  It's customizing and alteration, for the fun of it.  Show off your handiwork and build (or buy) a car that expresses your personality or whatever.  Songman, I have no problem with what you described you're doing.<P>For the last couple of hours I was thinking about starting a topic to suggest we come up with another name to replace "rice", "riceboyz", etc.  I don't like the racism of it either.  Thanks for speaking up Count_iblis.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000026||qwikgta||01-10-2001||07:53 PM||||I LOVE RICE....I love cars, have owned many.. My last project was a 79 Grand Am, I pulled the 301, put in a 400.  It had a  86 Trans Am rear spoiler, Trans am 16" inch rims, a 77 TA Hood scoop, 85 Fiero buckets, Monte Carlo SS quick ratio steering box...I could go on and on.  To me it was "The 79 GTO Pontiac never made".  <P>I plan to RICE my 88 to the max.  Big ol' rear spoiler, 17" rims, 3.4L motor, nice paint etc... It will turn heads.  I just put a set of GT rims (Black center) and FORMULA stickers on it last month.  Some engine chrome and a few cheap interior mods... I hope to have some more done for the summer FOCOA show this summer. I have a full set of poly going on, new shocks and springs and will score a swaybar soon.  After the engine change it will be better than a Formula.  (If i could have gotten a formula, I would not be doing all this to it, I would have fixed it up ALL STOCK.)<P>Stock is great..I love stock muscle cars and rare original stuff (88 GT, Formula, Indy) but my 88 only has the T-Top going for it, yea its rare but it is just a base coupe, it will never be worth much.  <P>My $.02<P>Rob <BR>  robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top||||reg||1
Z||000027||MrPBody||01-10-2001||07:59 PM||||I'm more likely to remove trim than to add it.  But hey, that's my thing.  Rather than pretend it's a GT, I'd prefer that observers say "That's nice.  What the hell <I>is</I> it?" (The Q-ship school of body mods.)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000028||mshill||01-10-2001||08:04 PM||||I find this whole discussion amusing.  Call and badge your car whatever/however you like.  People who know fieros will know what it is and people who don't know fieros won't give a rats behind what it is.<P>My 86GT that is going through the transformation to a Ferrari F50 will have all the Ferrari badging, floormats and prancing horses all over the place.  Would it ever pass for a real Ferrari?  No way, primarily because the license plate will read "FAUX F50".  The other easy way to tell will be that I will be getting out of it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>If personalizing your car is ricey then "I think I'm turning Japanese.  Yes, I think so..."<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Songman||01-10-2001||08:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jerpro:<BR><B>About the white fiero. It is a cool project, But I would of grabbed an indy and restored it instead.<BR>Basically the fake indy is a great car BUT I am against it. (this is opinion, no flame war intended)</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Just to be clear... I bought a real Indy and that is what gave me the idea to make an Indy clone. I want to do things to it that I would never do to a real Indy... I will have both. My true Indy that is oh so cool to look at, and my personalized Indy clone that will be a neck breaking road raging fun car to drive!<P>And there is no danger of a flame war. Each time I post I always make the point that everyone has their opinion and that is what matters to them. The main thing is that we all have fun. That's why I'm here....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon7.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000030||Sleeper||01-10-2001||09:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ChadMan:<BR><B><BR>If you've done enough mods that you feel your car warrants a new model designation, why not borrow one from newer Pontiacs?  A Fiero GT with a turbo might be a Fiero GTP.  A Fiero SE with a 3.8 might be an SSE.  This is creative, attracts attention at shows, and is not dishonest in any way.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll second that, when Chris West drops my 3.8 in I'm thinking about getting a GT-S or GT2, or geez Fiero F1 just something differant...good idea Chadman. <P>[QUOTE]Originally posted by qwikgta:<BR>[B]I LOVE RICE....I plan to RICE my 88 to the max.  Big ol' rear spoiler, 17" rims, 3.4L motor, nice paint etc... It will turn heads.  <BR> <BR>do it man, i'm down for it too, just not mega ricer. your fiero will be the sh*t, if you do it right it will be so dope.||||reg||1
Z||000031||DaRkLoRD||01-10-2001||11:58 PM||||I'd written a big long post about how there's a big difference between customizing and "ricey" customizing, but I realized it wasn't worth it.. Basically.. I like modifications.. but if someone puts something on their car that implies it's something it's not, then I disagree. This doesn't apply to kits however, as they're in a whole class by themselves. Ask anyone who's ever put a lot of work into a kit. it's a lot different than slapping a couple of stickers on "for looks".<P>btw, I agree with the count.. I'm open to suggestions for a new term for the coffecan wearing, stickered up wannabes..<P><BR>anyway, if I keep this up I'm gonna tick some people off.. so I'll shut up now.. I'm not really the kind of person who likes starting arguments.. sorry...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>(Cliff, feel free to close this topic if you feel it's necessary)<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||9
Z||000032||Cheever2||01-11-2001||12:03 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR>btw, I agree with the count.. I'm open to suggestions for a new term for the coffecan wearing, stickered up wannabes..<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>"Pretenders"???<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000033||William||01-11-2001||02:33 AM||||My take on this.....Personally I don't care for completely converting a car into another model, and adding the wrong badges. I'm doing something a little different. What I think of as the perfect fiero was never produced. Therefore, I'm in the process of building it using parts from several types of fieros along with certian custom parts. Kinda like going back in time and joining that Fiero design team. I don't want my car to look like it was customized, (of course us fiero lovers would know!), but rather like it could have came that way. I'm going for that "What the hell is that" look that was posted above. Here's what I'm doing........<P>I always liked the orginal red 84 se with a stick but rather have a V6. I was lucky enough to find a 85 SE v-6, so no engine swap was required and it got me of to a quick start.<P>Even tho I like body of the 84 SE coupe, I thought it needed a little more of an exotic look. A gt wing and ram air side scoops did the trick! The backwards rear deck scoop will be next. I think the coupe should of came that way stock!!!<BR> <BR>My favorite fiero interior includes speaker seats, 120 back lit gauges, aux gauges, leather, and a black / tan color. These items have been gathered and installed. The black / tan leather parts are being finshed this weekend!!!!<P>This is the type of thing I'm into...Not making a modified "looking" car or converting to another model, but rather contructing the Fiero that I wish had been produced.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000034||ur2biteme||01-11-2001||04:33 AM||||hey william, are you gonna put that air dam on that has been popping up on some of the pics of the 84-85 base coupes?  i'm not sure you know what i'm talking about, but it makes me almost want to change my '87 facias and find some ground f/x to match.  sounds like youve got a nice looking car in your head there.  <P>by the way i'm gonna use the term, but not to offend.  "rice" is more an attitude than anything.  i dont think any of what was mentioned before that us fourm members have done yet to be "rice" because we arent trying to deceive or belittle other car enthusiasts on the road.  it's the guy that pulls up next to me at the light, civic, cut springs, stickers from roof to tacky ground f/x, BAD negative camber, fart tip, decent intake, and that's it.  he thinks he's bad because his car is as loud as sitting inside a lawnmower.  i usually never race them unless i'm in the mood to do so (extremely rare, and more times than not, i'm just trying to merge and they wont let me in), but when i have, i've NEVER lost to one of these idiots in my DUKE!  now that's what i call "rice" or whatever P.C. term we come up for it.  <P>if your gonna look tacky, or have a fast looking car and the attitude that goes with it, you'd better have the mechanicals to back it up.  otherwise, enjoy the image and leave people that are trying to get from point A to point B alone.  i make fun of these guys all the time, but that's my freedom of expression, just like it's their freedom of expression to put that huge "powered by honda" banner across their windshield, like we'd forget and think it was made by ferarri or something. point is, they can do what they want, and we can think they are stupid.  it's what this country allows us to do.<P><I>Elvis has left the building</I><P><P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>170k awaiting a tranny:(<BR>http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme||||reg||1
Z||000035||DJRice||01-11-2001||10:05 PM||||We have an Silver '84 2m4 with the engine and tranny from an '85 2m4 (2.5L 5spd), a black hood from an '85, a silver engine compartment lid from an '88, backlight gauges, and seats from a 97 Camaro.  <P>Im proud to call that car "Riced" up!<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000036||DaRkLoRD||01-11-2001||10:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DJRice:<BR><B>We have an Silver '84 2m4 with the engine and tranny from an '85 2m4 (2.5L 5spd), a black hood from an '85, a silver engine compartment lid from an '88, backlight gauges, and seats from a 97 Camaro.  <P>Im proud to call that car "Riced" up!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I wouldn't call that even close to "ricey" (or any other PC term we come up with) it's just a customized fiero!<P>I think there are extremely diversified opinions on what we're talking about here.. if it's not pretending to be something it's not (this includes putting bigger tips on to make the car sound louder) it's a wannabe.. now, if the engine actually is souped up.. then it's not so bad. but a 5" tip on a stock engine/exhaust... is usually unnecessary..<P>For the record, I love modified Fieros.. I just consider a 4cyl coupe with V6 badging to be on the same level as a regular Integra with a VTEC sticker, or a 6cyl Mustang with a 5.0 badge...<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
